@prompt
In Hazel, you can create a list by writing its elements between square brackets, separated by commas. For example, `[1, 2, 3]` is a list of three integers.

The type of a list is written as `[T]` where `T` is the type of the elements. So `[1, 2, 3]` has type `[Int]`, and `["hello", "world"]` has type `[String]`. All elements in a list must have the same type.

Complete the let binding below so that `first_four` contains the first four positive integers: `[1, 2, 3, 4]`.

@hint
Fill in the list with the first four positive integers

@reference
### List Literal
```hazelnoeval
[1, 2, 3]
```

### List Type
`[Int]`, `[String]`, `[Bool]`

@hints
first_four should be [1, 2, 3, 4]

@code
let first_four : [Int] = [?] in
first_four

@test
test first_four == [1, 2, 3, 4] end
